Online\nSearch Properties on a Map\nFind Info on Properties\nSign up for Emergency Notifications\nFind us on Social Media\nSee Job Openings\nGive Feedback\nContact Us\nJerry Spruell\nDirector\nLocation\n201 St. Andrew St.\nSuite 434\nPO Box 10\nTarboro, NC 27886\nPhone: 252- 641-7852\nFax: 252-641-1991\nHours\n8am - 5pm\nMonday-Friday\nBoard of Elections\nAbout Us\nFAQs\nPoll Workers\nVoter ID Information\nVoter Registration\nOnline Voter Registration/Update\nVoter Information Lookup\nHistorical Election Data\nAbsentee Voting\nPolling Places\nMultipartisan Assistance Team (MAT)\nCampaign Finance Information\nCampaign Finance Records\nElection Results\nElected Officials\nBoard Meetings\nForms\nElectoral Maps\nResources\nEdgecombe County Elected Officials\nBoard of Elections\nHome\nDepartments\nBoard of Elections\nResponsibilities\nThe Edgecombe County Board of Elections has the responsibility of conducting all elections held within the County. In the BOE office we: register new voters; provide ballots and staffing for the voting precincts; maintain and update voter registrations by removing the names of the deceased, felons, and voters that have moved from the county; stay abreast of changes in election laws and regulations; and maintain campaign reports for candidates.\nMission Statement\nThe mission of the Edgecombe County Board of Elections is to administer fair, accurate, secure, accessible, and transparent elections while providing impartial, professional, and responsive service to all voters. We are committed to protecting the integrity of the electoral process, ensuring compliance with federal and North Carolina election laws, maintaining accurate voter registration records, and promoting public confidence through accountability, education, and excellence in election administration.\n2026 General Election Information\nNovember 2026 Candidate Detail List\nOfficial Summarv Explanation of 2026 Constitutional Amendments\nAn Absentee by Mail Ballot\nEarly Voting Dates and Locations\nAbsentee Meeting Dates\nOfficial Election Notices\n201 St. Andrew St. - PO Box 10\nTarboro, NC 27886\nPhone:\n(252) 641-7835\nHours: Monday-Friday: 8 AM - 5:00 PM\n\u00a9 2026 Edgecombe County, NC\n|\nPowered by\nrevize\n., the government website experts.\nLogin\nShare this page\nShare this page\nClose\nPlease ensure Javascript is enabled for purposes of\nwebsite accessibility",
